OMAT-SE

Faceted search over materials composition and property measurements.

Live
  Frontend       https://omat-se.vercel.app
  API reference  https://jayesh-dev21.github.io/Omat-se/

Repository
  apps/api       FastAPI service
  apps/mcp       MCP server (Python SDK)
  apps/web       Next.js UI, deployed on Vercel
  apps/workers   Async consumers (phase 2)
  packages/      Shared Python domain, ingestion CLI, typed TypeScript client
  data/          Source CSV, taxonomy, synonyms, staging
  infra/         Terraform and container placeholders
  docs/          Architecture, schema, ADRs, API reference
  report/        LaTeX write-up

Local setup
  cp .env.example .env
  cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
  just up
  just install
  just dev-api
  bun install
  just web-dev
  just docs      # local API reference on http://localhost:8080

Requirements: Python 3.11+, Bun, Docker.
Architecture: docs/architecture.md
Schema: docs/schema.md
License: MIT

Deploy
  Frontend
    Create a Vercel project with Root Directory `apps/web` and set
    NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL in the project environment variables. Vercel builds
    with `apps/web/vercel.json`; the install step runs from the repo root so
    the Bun workspace and `bun.lock` are used. You can deploy through Vercel's
    Git integration or `.github/workflows/deploy-web.yml` (add VERCEL_TOKEN,
    VERCEL_ORG_ID, and VERCEL_PROJECT_ID), not both.

  API reference
    `.github/workflows/docs.yml` generates `openapi.json` from FastAPI and
    publishes the Scalar shell in `docs/api` to GitHub Pages. Enable
    Settings -> Pages -> Source: GitHub Actions once, then push to `master`
    or run the workflow manually.
